---
import MarketingPreview from './MarketingPreview.astro';
import MarketingCopy from './MarketingCopy.astro';
import { renderLinkedIn } from '../../../scripts/marketing/renderers.mjs';
const { pack } = Astro.props;
const base = `/marketing/${pack.id}`;
const voices = [
  { key: 'opda', title: 'From the OPDA account', description: 'For authorised OPDA representatives publishing through OPDA’s account.' },
  { key: 'partner', title: 'From your organisation', description: 'For an organisation or interest group sharing the invitation without implying partnership or endorsement.' },
];
---
<p>These are designed campaign previews, not a LinkedIn editor. Upload the JPEG illustration or PNG infographic, then use <strong>View plain text</strong> to copy a selected post. The HTML is for reviewing and sharing the campaign outside LinkedIn. Add your own perspective and an image description before publishing.</p>
<div class="marketing-actions">
  <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={`${base}/images/social-card.jpg`} download>Download LinkedIn image · JPEG</a>
  <a class="btn" href={`${base}/images/contribution-infographic.png`} download>Download infographic · PNG</a>
  <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={`${base}/images/contribution-infographic.svg`} download>Download editable infographic · SVG</a>
</div>
{voices.map((voice) => <div class="marketing-voice">
  <h3>{voice.title}</h3><p>{voice.description}</p>
  <MarketingPreview id={`${pack.id}-${voice.key}-sequence`} title={`${pack.label} · ${voice.title}`} preview={`${base}/linkedin/${voice.key}.html`} plainText={false} />
  {pack.linkedin[voice.key].posts.map((post, index) => <MarketingCopy id={`${pack.id}-${voice.key}-${post.id}`} title={`${index + 1}. ${post.title}`} text={renderLinkedIn(pack, voice.key, post)} download={`${base}/linkedin/${voice.key}-${String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}-${post.id}.txt`} rows={10} />)}
</div>)}
